          "(a) The ER is a winding network of thin membranous sacs found in close association with the cell nucleus. (b) Rough endoplasmic reticulum (c) Smooth endoplasmic reticulum.",
          "Endoplasmic reticulum can exist in two forms: Rough endoplasmic reticulum and smooth endoplasmic reticulum (Figure 1.9). These two types of endoplasmic reticulum perform some very different functions and can be found in very different amounts depending on the type of the cell. Rough endoplasmic reticulum is so called because its membrane is dotted with embedded granules organelles called \u2018ribosomes\u2019, giving the rough endoplasmic reticulum a bumpy appearance.",
          "The Golgi apparatus: The Golgi apparatus (Figure 1.10) is responsible for sorting, modifying, and shipping off the products that come from the rough endoplasmic reticulum, much like a post-office. The Golgi apparatus looks like stacked flattened discs, almost like stacks of oddly shaped pancakes. The Golgi apparatus has two distinct sides, each with a different role. One side of the apparatus receives products in vesicles. These products are sorted through the apparatus, and then they are released from the opposite side after being repackaged into new vesicles. If the product is to be exported from the cell, the vesicle migrates to the cell surface and fuses to the cell membrane, and the cargo is secreted."
