          "Alveolar cells or pneumocytes: Which are of two types namely type I alveolar cells and type II alveolar cells (Figure 4.8). Type I alveolar cells are the squamous epithelial cells forming about 95% of the total number of cells. These cells from the site of gas exchange between the alveolus and the blood. Type II alveolar cells are cuboidal in nature and form about 5% of alveolar cells. These cells are also called \u2018granular pneumocytes\u2019. Type II alveolar cells secrete alveolar fluid and surfactant.",
