          "Parotid glands",
          "Sub maxillary or submandibular glands",
          "Sublingual glands",
          "Parotid glands: Largest of all salivary glands, situated at the side of the face just below and in front of the ear. Each gland weighs about 20 to 30 grams in adults. Secretions from these glands are emptied into the oral cavity by Stensen duct and this duct is about 35 mm to 40mm long and opens inside the cheek against the upper second molar tooth.",
          "Submaxillary glands: Submaxillary glands or submandibular glands are located in Submaxillary triangle; medial to mandible. Each gland weighs about 8 to 10 gram. Saliva from these glands is emptied into the oral cavity by Wharton duct, which is about 40 mm long. The duct opens at the side of frenulum of tongue, by means of a small opening on the summit of papilla called \u2018caruncula sublingualis\u2019.",
          "Figure 5.6: Salivary Glands.",
          "Sublingual glands: Sublingual glands are the smallest salivary glands situated in the mucosa at the floor of the mouth. Each gland weighs about 2 to 3 g. Saliva from these glands is poured into 5 to 15 small ducts called \u2018ducts of rivinus\u2019. These ducts open on small papillae beneath the tongue. One of the ducts is larger and it is called \u2018Bartholin duct\u2019.",
