        "clinicalPearl": "**Clinical Pearl:** Appendicitis: Inflammation of appendix is known as \u2018appendicitis\u2019. Appendix is a small, worm like appendage, projecting from cecum of ascending colon. It is situated on the lower right side of the abdomen. Appendix does not have any function in human beings. But, it can create major problems when diseased. Appendicitis can develop at any age. However, it is very common between 10 and 30 years of age",
