          "Bile canaliculi: These are small ducts between hepatocytes that collect bile produced by the hepatocytes. From bile canaliculi, bile passes into bile ductules and then bile ducts. The bile ducts merge and eventually form the larger right and left hepatic ducts, which unite and exit the liver as the common hepatic duct. The common hepatic duct joins the cystic duct from the gallbladder to form the common bile duct. Then, the bile enters from the small intestine to participate in digestion.",
