        "clinicalPearl": "**Clinical Pearl:** Constipation: Failure of voiding of feces, which produces discomfort, is known as \u2018constipation\u2019. It is due to the lack of movements necessary for defecation. Due to the absence of mass movement in colon, feces remain in the large intestine for a long time, resulting in absorption of fluid. So the feces become hard and dry.",
