          "Epidermis: The epidermis is the outer layer of skin. The thickness of the epidermis (Figure: 11.12) varies in different types of skin. It is the thinnest on the eyelids at .05 mm and thickest on the palms and sole at 1.5 mm.",
          "The epidermis contains 5 layers. From bottom to top the layers are named.",
