        "id": "subj-anat-7-76",
        "question": "Shape, size, and direction: Classification of muscles by their shapes, e.g., the\u00a0deltoids\u00a0has a delta or triangular shape. The serratus muscles feature a serrated or saw-like shape. The rhomboid major is a rhombus or diamond shape. The size of the muscle can be used to distinguish between two muscles found in the same region.",
        "answer": "INC standard: Detail anatomical landmarks, physiological mechanisms, and clinical nursing management for Shape, size, and direction: Classification of muscles by their shapes, e.g., the\u00a0deltoids\u00a0has a delta or triangular shape. The serratus muscles feature a serrated or saw-like shape. The rhomboid major is a rhombus or diamond shape. The size of the muscle can be used to distinguish between two muscles found in the same region..",
