        "answer": "INC standard: Detail anatomical landmarks, physiological mechanisms, and clinical nursing management for Triceps brachii: is the only muscle of the posterior arm. It has three heads that attach to the scapula and humerus, and it inserts on the ulna. The triceps extends the forearm. It is sometimes called the ' boxer\u2019s muscle because it extends the elbow when a punch is thrown. The triceps is also used in tennis to do a back hand volley..",
