          "Anatomical position of the kidney: The kidneys are excretory organs situated on posterior abdominal wall one on each side of the vertebral column behind the peritoneum and below the diaphragm extend from the 12th thoracic to the 3rd lumbar vertebrae receiving some protection from the lower rib cage. The right kidney is lower than the left because it is crowded by the liver.",
          "Size of kidney: They are about 11-14 cm. in length, 6 cm. wide and 3 cm. thick.",
          "Weight of of the kidney: Each adult kidney weighs about 125-175 gram in males and 115-155 gram in females.",
          "Shape  of the kidney: The kidneys are a pair of reddish brown, bean-shaped organ (Figure 7.2). The bean shape of the kidney is medially concave and laterally convex. They are roughly the size of our fist, and the male kidney is typically a bit larger than the female kidney.",
          "Coverings of the kidney: The kidney has three coverings",
