          "Lymphatic Drainage of the Penis: Internal iliac node.",
          "Nerve Supply to the Penis: Sensory pudendal nerve, sympathetic fibers and parasympathetic fibers.",
          "Bulbourethral Glands: Located near the base of the penisbelow the prostate. Pea shaped organ. The final addition to semen is made by  the bulbourethral glands (Cowper\u2019s glands)  are a pair of glands small, about the size of a pea, and located near the base of the penisbelow the prostate. A short duct from each enters the proximal end of the penile urethra. In response to sexual stimulation, the bulbourethral glands secrete a clear mucous an alkaline substance to help protect and transport the sperm.",
          "Structure of Sperm: The sperm in human beings is a highly specialized structure. Also called \u2018male gamete\u2019, several thousand of them are produced and contained in fluid called \u2018semen\u2019 before it is transferred to the female for the process of fertilization. A mature sperm also called \u2018spermatozoa\u2019 (Figure 8.11). A\u00a0mature human sperm cell has snake like structure. It has following parts - head, neck, middle piece and tail.",
