          "The Penis has 3 parts: a root, body (shaft), and glans penis (Figure 8.10).",
          "Root: base of the penis, which extends into the pelvis and attaches to the pelvic muscles. The body is the visible, pendant portion.  Shaft or body of the penis divided into sections of tissue called \u2018corpora\u2019. Corpora cavernosa is larger, upper level of tissue and corpora spongiosum, smaller, lower level of tissue which contains the urethra.",
          "Glans penis: The corpus spongiosum expands at the distal end (tip) to form the glans penis which is expanded triangular structure. Has a high concentration of nerve endings, resulting in very sensitive skin that influences the likelihood of ejaculation the urethra, which extends throughout the length of the corpus spongiosum, open is through the external urethral orifice at the tip of the glans penis. The skin from the shaft extends down over the glans and forms a collar called the \u2018prepuce\u2019 (or foreskin). This is sometimes removed by circumcision. The foreskin also contains a dense concentration of nerve endings, and both lubricate and protect the sensitive skin of the glans penis."
