        "id": "sec-anat-9-18",
        "title": "Female Reproductive System",
        "content": [
          "The female reproductive system (Figure 8.12) includes the ovaries, fallopian tubes, uterus, vagina, vulva, and breasts. These organs are involved in the production and transportation of gametes and the production of sex hormones. The female reproductive system (Figure 8.13) also facilitates the fertilization of ova by sperm and supports the development of offspring during pregnancy and infancy. One of the primary directives of life is to reproduce and pass on genetic information to future generations. This is the purpose of the human reproductive system. Male and female both carry half of the genetic information required to produce a human, both contain a number of the same hormones and both have similar stages of reproductive development.",
          "Figure 8.12 Female reproductive systems."
        ],
