          "1709530110959",
          "Figure 8.18: Ligaments of uterus.",
          "Broad ligament: These are formed by double layer of peritoneum. Blood vessels, lymphatic and nerves pass to the uterus between the layers of broad ligaments.",
          "Round ligament: These are two fibrous bands which lie between the two layers of broad ligaments. They extends from then uterus, pass through the inguinal canal and the end in subcutaneous tissue of labia majora.",
